      "value": "paywalling a feature which should be there for everybody is not the way.\n\nthis would not be beneficial for either party because avatar creators would be restricted in what shaders they can use, and vrchat would likely get round 2 of backlash after doing something insanely stupid.\n\naditionally, doing a \"brief scan before loading an avatar\" is only adding more on top of the already long list of things that happen when avatars load, thus making them load even slower than they already are.\n\non top of that: Quest shaders have been suggested numerous times. so far, the response has always been no, and the furthest we've gotten is \"tracked\" on \"Whitelist Unity Chan Toon Shader 2 for PC and Quest.\".\n\nas a final point why this is completely braindead:\n\nNobody would want their own looks to be dependant on if others pay for something that you wouldn't benefit from.\n\nAs avatar creators, we usually would like everybody to see our creations as pretty and cool as they can be, and bringing this bullshit to VRC would be the exact opposite of what everybody wants.",
